@integrations/skills/sigil/external-guidance-evidence.sigil import { ExternalGuidanceEvidence }

component SigilDesignConversation {
  goal {
    Guide a user from incomplete software intent to a coherent contract through small, material decisions.

    Surface unknowns, conflicts, alternatives, and pitfalls without replacing user decision authority.
  }

  interface {
    DecisionConversation {
      begins from user intent and relevant evidence

      presents one primary material decision per turn unless the user requests grouped review

      explains why the decision matters, available alternatives, their consequences, and a reasoned recommendation

      acknowledges each answer and states its effect on the emerging contract
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      enters a dedicated same-chat correction phase when review identifies a material semantic, architectural, or design problem

      warns the user by naming the exact problem, supporting evidence, likely consequences, and risk

      asks one focused clarification or correction decision at a time

      offers concrete resolution options, their trade-offs, and a reasoned recommendation

      returns to ordinary design work only after the problem is resolved
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      maintains confirmed, provisionally assumed, intentionally deferred, and unresolved decisions

      summarizes agreed decisions, remaining blockers, deferrals, and conflicts
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      produces exact proposed Sigil only after every blocking decision is resolved
    }
  }
}

expand SigilDesignConversation {
  state {
    DecisionConversation {
      Conversation phase is framing, exploring, resolving, synthesizing, or awaiting approval.

      An unresolved decision is blocking when it could materially change the contract.
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      A correction finding is suspected, confirmed, or resolved.

      A suspected or confirmed material problem keeps the conversation in correction.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      A material decision is confirmed, provisionally assumed, intentionally deferred, or unresolved.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      Synthesis readiness requires no blocking unresolved decision.
    }
  }

  logic {
    DecisionConversation {
      Classify questions by their effect on purpose, boundary, ownership, behavior, lifecycle, architecture, risk, and verification.

      Ask the unresolved question whose answer most strongly shapes later decisions.

      After each answer, restate the resulting decision and identify dependent questions or conflicts.

      When the user is uncertain, present a conservative recommendation and permit only non-blocking uncertainty to be deferred.
    }

    ApplicabilityAssessment {
      Complete basic framing before assessing whether external guidance could materially affect the next design decision.

      Invoke ExternalGuidanceEvidence before presenting alternatives or a recommendation for a guidance-sensitive material decision.

      Reassess applicability when the boundary, risk, environment, or binding requirements change.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      Use applicable evidence to explain alternatives, consequences, uncertainty, and the reasoned recommendation.

      Treat disagreement between authoritative sources as an unresolved design constraint when no project decision exists.

      Enter CorrectionConversation when applicable guidance materially conflicts with approved Sigil or a confirmed user decision.

      Offer a conservative provisional option only when incomplete evidence affects a low-risk reversible decision.

      Require missing evidence or qualified review before recommending a definitive high-risk or compliance-critical choice.
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      When review identifies a material semantic, architectural, or design problem, pause ordinary design exploration and enter the same-chat correction phase.

      Separate exact Sigil evidence, repository evidence, and inference before describing a finding as a mistake.

      Explain how the problem could affect contracts, ownership, lifecycle, security, persistence, interoperability, verification, or implementation.

      Recommend a correction, present meaningful alternatives and trade-offs, and ask which intent should govern.

      Update the decision ledger after each answer and resume ordinary design work only when the problem is resolved.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      Record each answer with its decision state and effect on unresolved blockers.

      Preserve intentionally deferred decisions in every checkpoint and final synthesis.

      Reopen a confirmed decision only when new evidence conflicts with it.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      When no blockers remain, summarize confirmed, provisional, deferred, and unresolved decisions before presenting exact Sigil.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    DecisionConversation {
      Each question materially improves the resulting contract.

      Independent questions are not presented as an exhaustive questionnaire.

      The user remains the authority for product, architecture, permission, risk, and tradeoff decisions.

      Immaterial hypothetical edge cases are not pursued merely for completeness.
    }

    ApplicabilityAssessment {
      External-guidance research follows sufficient framing and does not run before every conversational question.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      Evidence informs the conversation without replacing user decision authority.

      Research uncertainty may keep a material decision unresolved but does not create an independent approval gate.

      A valid packet may be reused without repeated research while its invalidation conditions remain unchanged.
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      A subjective preference is not labeled a problem without concrete semantic or risk evidence.

      The affected Sigil is not silently corrected while the user is deciding the intended resolution.

      A confirmed material problem cannot be deferred, treated as a provisional assumption, or bypassed for implementation.

      User resolution of the problem does not replace the existing Sigil proposal and approval gates.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      Provisional assumptions remain visible and do not become confirmed decisions implicitly.

      A blocking unresolved decision cannot be intentionally deferred.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      Exact Sigil is not synthesized while any blocking decision remains unresolved.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ApplicabilityAssessment {
      Decision: Use just-in-time ExternalGuidanceEvidence after minimum framing and before guidance-sensitive alternatives or recommendations.

      Scope: Governs Sigil design conversation; excludes initial purpose and boundary discovery that must precede meaningful applicability assessment.

      Trade-offs: Some design turns pause for research before presenting the next decision.

      Design issues addressed: Deferring research until final standards review produces weaker questions and can omit relevant alternatives or constraints.

      Consequences: Evidence improves decision framing without turning research into a conversational or approval gate.

      Revisit when: Evidence acquisition cannot complete within an interactive design conversation.
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      Decision: Use a dedicated correction phase within the same chat for suspected or confirmed material semantic, architectural, or design problems.

      Scope: Governs Sigil design and review conversations; excludes immaterial preferences and unrelated user discussions.

      Trade-offs: Pausing ordinary design questions adds conversational latency.

      Design issues addressed: Material mistakes and risks could otherwise be mentioned without requiring focused user resolution.

      Consequences: Affected Sigil remains unchanged and unrelated design work pauses until the problem is resolved.

      Revisit when: Host conversation isolation or safety requirements make a separate thread necessary.
    }
  }

  cases {
    DecisionConversation {
      A vague product idea begins with intended outcome and users rather than implementation technology.

      A conflict with an earlier answer is explained before another topic begins.

      An uncertain user receives a recommendation with consequences rather than an unexplained default.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      A version-sensitive framework choice cites matching official documentation while explaining alternatives.

      Conflicting guidance is presented as uncertainty rather than disguised as a confident recommendation.

      Missing compliance-critical evidence keeps the affected decision unresolved pending qualified review.
    }

    CorrectionConversation {
      Contradictory ownership claims trigger a warning, risk explanation, and focused correction decision before proposal synthesis.

      An architectural cycle that creates unclear lifecycle ownership blocks implementation until the user selects a resolution.

      Ambiguous failure behavior with materially different observable outcomes is clarified before Sigil is approved.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      An intentionally deferred non-blocking decision remains visible in the synthesis.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      A permission, destructive-behavior, or public-contract ambiguity blocks exact Sigil and implementation.
    }
  }
}
